 # Monorepo and Tooling

- Prefer workspace-aware commands; the client uses npm scripts defined in `Client/package.json`.
- Do not edit files in `Client/dist/`, `Client/coverage/`, or `Client/playwright-report/` (generated outputs).
- Follow documented structure in **`documentation/`**: see `documentation/README.md`, `documentation/client/README.md`, and `documentation/HOW_WE_DOCUMENT.md`. Client architecture and package layout are in `documentation/client/` and `Client/ARCHITECTURE.md`. For Thin App (Fat Packages) — apps as composition layer only — see `documentation/client/thin-app-architecture.md` and `thin-app-architecture.mdc`.
- Keep configuration changes in `Client/config/` where applicable (ESLint, Prettier, PostCSS) and root configs for Vite/Tailwind/TS.
- For CI or local tasks, use existing scripts: dev, build, test, test:e2e, lint, format.
- **NEVER create markdown files (.md, .mdc, .markdown) unless explicitly requested by the user**, except: (1) adding or updating lightweight README.md in major top-level folders (Client, Server, documentation) per `documentation/HOW_WE_DOCUMENT.md`, or (2) adding docs under `documentation/client/` or `documentation/server/` when the user asks for documentation.

